    "name": "pyvoa: Python Virus Open Analysis",
    "description": "pyvoa is an open-source Python library providing unified access to epidemiological databases (COVID-19 and other viral datasets), a standardised data format, transparent joins with geolocation databases, and built-in tools for time-series and cartographic visualisation. It is designed to be usable by non-specialists — high-school and university students, science journalists, researchers unfamiliar with data extraction — while remaining scriptable for advanced Python users.",
